        {
          "paragraph": 3,
          "status": "verbatim-korean-new-english-translation",
          "sourceExcerpt": "contextual-death",
          "sourcePages": "432",
          "english": "The important point here is that deep-learning embeddings can vary with context. Even the same word, death, can be drawn toward a history cluster in Gloucester’s speech because its sense of legal punishment is strong. In another scene, however, when death emphasizes loss and fear, it moves closer to the tragedy cluster. Such contextual embeddings capture a word not as a fixed sign but as a trajectory of meaning moving within context. This makes them particularly suitable for categories such as genre that change through relationships.",
          "koreanSHA256": "07665444fa882cc25bdc454e5f9fb0a5fa4a76781db212f7f05ffe33184e8682"
        }
      ]
    },
