          "paragraph": 3,
          "status": "verbatim-korean-new-english-translation",
          "sourceExcerpt": "representation-and-learning",
          "sourcePages": "434–435",
          "english": "First distinguish the roles of embedding and pretraining. Embedding refers to the technical form of representing words, sentences or scenes as numeric vectors: high-dimensional arrays of real numbers. In other words, embedding converts textual meaning into coordinates consisting of hundreds of numbers. These numbers do not contain meaning from the outset. At initialization, each word vector is set to nearly random values and is merely a combination of computable numbers. Pretraining is the learning process that makes these initially meaningless arrays reflect patterns of actual language use. If embedding is a vessel for meaning, pretraining repeatedly adjusts it so that the vessel acquires linguistic content.",
          "koreanSHA256": "8caec80adb00ad1e3a0c9a9e7590253d988f6019dd01644aa88ca03a5c97f617"
        }
